e role(s) per compat.roles (${Object.entries(roles).map(([f, t]) => `${f}→${t}`).join(\",\")})`);\n                        // Kiro: remember which items the BUILT-IN map re-voiced, so the\n                        // invariant judge can see bili's own injected prompt as what it is\n                        // (a developer item) instead of an unexplained user insertion.\n                        if (Object.keys(builtin).length > 0) judgeRoleRestore = builtinRoleRestorePoints(body, protocol, builtin, roles);\n                    }\n                } else {\n                    const applied = applyCompatRoles(body, protocol, roles);\n                    if (applied.rewritten > 0) {\n                        wireBody = applied.body;\n                        log(\"info\", `[${prepared?.session.id ?? \"passthrough\"}] [compat] rewrote ${applied.rewritten} message role(s) per compat.roles (${Object.entries(roles).map(([f, t]) => `${f}→${t}`).join(\",\")})`);\n                        // Kiro: remember which items the BUILT-IN map re-voiced, so the\n                        // invariant judge can see bili's own injected prompt as what it is\n                        // (a developer item) instead of an unexplained user insertion.\n                        if (Object.keys(builtin).length > 0) judgeRoleRestore = builtinRoleRestorePoints(body, protocol, builtin, roles);\n                    }\n                    // Unchanged bytes keep the prepare-time binding honest; a rewrite\n                    // here came from an independent parse, so no carrier lineage can\n                    // be proven against it — ownership is UNKNOWN from here on.\n                    if (applied.rewritten > 0) invalidateSeparatorOwnership();\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        // #1093 land output-side compression AFTER every other body mutation (compat\n        // above) so the turn classifier sees the final message list. All wires, not\n        // just the compat pair; idempotent, byte-identical when nothing changes.\n        steerProtocol = protocol;\n        if (steerCfg && steerCfg.enabled && typeof wireBody === \"string\") {\n            // #564/#2627: same object-graph rule as the role rewrite above — when a\n            // manifest rides this turn, the steering must land on the carriers' own\n            // graph so the claims can be re-anchored instead of dropped.\n            const graph = separatorManifest !== undefined ? wireGraph() : null;\n            if (graph !== null) {\n                const labels = applyOutputSteeringJson(graph, protocol, steerCfg);\n                if (labels.length > 0) {\n                    commitGraph();\n                    log(\"info\", `[${prepared?.session.id ?? \"passthrough\"}] [output-steering] applied (${labels.join(\", \")})`);\n                }\n            } else {\n                const applied = applyOutputSteering(wireBody, protocol, steerCfg);\n                if (applied.changed) {\n                    wireBody = applied.body;\n                    invalidateSeparatorOwnership();\n                    log(\"info\", `[${prepared?.session.id ?? \"passthrough\"}] [output-steering] applied (${applied.labels.join(\", \")})`);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        // #1757: compat.dropFields — AFTER every other body mutation (roles,\n        // output steering) so the final shape carries the drops, BEFORE the\n        // #1421 outbound stamp whose digest must cover the exact forwarded\n        // bytes. Protocol-neutral (any JSON-object body), unlike the role\n        // rewrite above which is openai/responses-only.\n        compatDropPaths = resolveCompatDropFields(opts.routes, upstreamUrl, opts.compat?.dropFields);\n        if (compatDropPaths.length > 0 && typeof wireBody === \"string\") {\n            // #564/#2627: drops run on the SAME graph as every other transform, so\n            // identity decides — not the drop path's shape. A drop that deletes or\n            // rewrites a carrier simply removes it from the identity Map (or fails\n            // isSeparatorCarrier), while carriers it never touches keep their object\n            // identity and re-anchor. No path pattern is pre-judged.\n            const graph = separatorManifest !== undefined ? wireGraph() : null;\n            if (graph !== null) {\n                const dropped = dropCompatFieldsJson(graph, compatDropPaths);\n                if (dropped > 0) {\n                    commitGraph();\n                    log(\"info\", `[${prepared?.session.id ?? \"passthrough\"}] [compat] dropped ${dropped} field(s) per compat.dropFields (${compatDropPaths.join(\", \")}) (#1757)`);\n                }\n            } else {\n                const applied = applyCompatDropFields(wireBody, compatDropPaths);\n                if (applied.dropped > 0) {\n                    wireBody = applied.body;\n                    invalidateSeparatorOwnership();\n                    log(\"info\", `[${prepared?.session.id ?? \"passthrough\"}] [compat] dropped ${applied.dropped} field(s) per compat.dropFields (${compatDropPaths.join(\", \")}) (#1757)`);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    // #1295: restore the CLI envelope at the final forward boundary — AFTER\n    // every flat-body mutation above (compat roles, output steering) so the\n    // client's provider plugin receives its exact native shape.\n    if (prepared?.commandcode && typeof wireBody === \"string\") {\n        try {\n            wireBody = JSON.stringify(rewrapCommandcodeBody(JSON.parse(wireBody) as Record<string, unknown>, prepared.commandcode.meta));\n        } catch { /* malformed flat body — pass through unchanged */ }\n    }\n    // zed cloud wire: same final-boundary rewrap for the /completions envelope.\n    if (prepared?.zed && typeof wireBody === \"string\") {\n        try {\n            wireBody = JSON.stringify(rewrapZedEnvelope(JSON.parse(wireBody) as Record<string, unknown>, prepared.zed.meta));\n        } catch { /* malformed inner body — pass through unchanged */ }\n    }\n    // #1421/#1683: outbound chain checkpoint — when egress stamping is enabled\n    // (chainEgressStamp, DEFAULT OFF), every request THIS instance actually\n    // processed leaves with a request-level stamp, so a downstream bili applies\n    // first-processor-wins even when x-bili-hop was stripped in transit. The\n    // carrier is model-visible (insertCheckpointCarrier), which is why this is\n    // opt-in: models read it as phantom user input and burn tokens on it. Lands\n    // AFTER compat roles + output steering: the digest must cover the exact\n    // bytes forwarded. Best-effort — a stamp failure never breaks the forward.\n    // Passthrough/side/forge/classifier forwards carry no stamp: only a real\n    // kernel pass (processedMessages non-empty — side/classifier Prepareds are\n    // empty) claims processing, per the first-processor-wins contract. Inbound\n    // recognition + hop passthrough are unaffected by this switch.\n    if (prepared && !prepared.sidePassthrough && prepared.processedMessages.length > 0 && typeof wireBody === \"string\" && opts.chainEgressStamp === true) {\n        try {\n            // #564/#2627: stamp the SAME graph the manifest's carriers live in when\n            // one is riding this turn — `insertCheckpointCarrier` allocates a new\n            // input array but copies every other item by reference, so the carriers\n            // survive and are re-indexed at their shifted positions. The digest is\n            // computed over the graph, whose only difference from the parse is the\n            // dropped `undefined`-valued keys a raw parse would render back as null.\n            // When a manifest is riding this turn but the trusted graph is gone,\n            // the carriers' lineage is unprovable: stamp the plain parse for the\n            // upstream's sake, but record ownership as UNKNOWN rather than\n            // republishing bytes whose sepa