yload still over window ${limit} by local estimate (~${Math.round(result.payloadEstimate)} tok, ${result.compressedRanges} range(s) folded) ${viaNativeFit ? `but the outbound view (~${Math.round(outboundCalibrated)} tok) + clamped output budget ${outboundBudgetTokens ?? 0} fits the native window ${resolvedNativeWindow}` : \"with no upstream evidence\"} — forwarding once for the upstream to arbitrate size before failing fast (#3146/#4185)`);\n            return outbound;\n        }\n    }\n    // The payload still overflows the window: fail fast with a diagnostic\n    // error instead of forwarding a guaranteed-400 payload (#301).\n    // #3461 problem 2: DETERMINISTIC exhaustion (futile-round math proved no\n    // combination of folds can close the gap regardless of upstream health)\n    // can never succeed for this identical payload — answer it 413 like every\n    // other \"can never fit as-is\" verdict (#2847 lesson applied to the\n    // exhaustion path; #2921/#3146 doomed-bytes precedent) instead of 502,\n    // which status-code-driven headless hosts read as transient and spin on\n    // forever (field measurement: 5+ doomed rounds). Relay-dependent\n    // exhaustion (empty/truncated/incomplete summaries, budget draws, pool\n    // saturation) stays 502: those walks succeed once the relay recovers.\n    // AND only when bili's own calibrated meter agrees the payload is over the\n    // window (!payloadFitsWindow): when the calibrated estimate FITS but the\n    // walk still ran (char-count trigger arm, overflow-armed baseline), the\n    // doom is a relay-billing artifact bili cannot compute (#496/#767/#857\n    // byte-relay lanes) — bili must not declare structural doom for it; those\n    // lanes keep their 502 fail-fast contract where NOT re-forwarding IS the\n    // protection, not a client spin.\n    // Identity fast path, final net: a DETERMINISTIC exhaustion (futile-round\n    // math — no combination of folds closes the gap, #3461 problem 2) would\n    // answer 413 by the mapping below. For an identified session with\n    // same-origin+model upstream reality, that local doom-math is exactly the\n    // judgment the incident showed unreliable — forward the outbound instead.\n    // Relay-dependent (non-deterministic) exhaustion keeps its 502: that is\n    // bili's own summary relay failing, not a payload verdict.\n    if (trustedForward && f?.kind === \"exhausted\" && f.deterministic) {\n        log(\"warn\", `[${session.id}] identity fast path: fold walk exhausted deterministically — upstream reality (~${session.stats.lastInputTokens} tok, ${evidenceSource} on this origin+model) outranks the local doom-math; forwarding the outbound as configured (a genuine 400 arms the overflow recovery)`);\n        return outbound;\n    }\n    // #7537 (owner ruling 2026-11-22): a DETERMINISTIC size exhaustion used to\n    // answer 413 — a LOCAL estimate verdict that the ruling supersedes: fold\n    // as far as the walk gets, then FORWARD; the upstream answers with its\n    // own real numbers (annotated in relay.ts). Only relay-side failures keep\n    // a local refusal: the summary relay itself is down (non-deterministic\n    // exhaustion → 502) or the relay hit an upstream 429 (→ 503).\n    if (f?.kind === \"exhausted\" && f.deterministic && !payloadFitsWindow) {\n        if (statedWall > 0) {\n            // Evidence-based refusal — the one local 413 that survives the\n            // #7537 estimate-refusal ruling: the UPSTREAM itself proved this\n            // wall (a stated overflow number, or its own 400/413 arming at\n            // ~statedWall tok), the futile-round math proves no combination of\n            // folds can close the gap, and bili's calibrated meter agrees the\n            // payload is over the window. This is upstream evidence, not a\n            // local estimate (#3461/#496/#767/#857) — re-forwarding unchanged\n            // bytes would only re-burn the wire and re-teach the same wall.\n            noteLocalRefusal(session, currentOrigin, model, limit);\n            log(\"warn\", `[${session.id}] preflight fail-fast 413 (retryable=false): deterministic size exhaustion against a PROVEN window (~${statedWall.toLocaleString(\"en-US\")} tok upstream evidence; local estimate ~${Math.round(result.payloadEstimate)} tok after ${result.compressedRanges} fold(s), window ${limit}) — refusing locally; estimate-based refusals are gone (#7537) but this one is upstream evidence (#3461/#496)`);\n            return failFast(413, f?.detail ?? \"the payload still exceeds the window after preflight compression — the upstream has already proved this wall and nothing more can fold\", false, result.compressedRanges > 0 ? foldedCalibratedSize : undefined, result.rangesRemaining);\n        }\n        const fwdMsgs = outbound.processedMessages.length > 0 ? outbound.processedMessages : outbound.originalMessages;\n        log(\"warn\", `[${session.id}] fold walk exhausted deterministically (nothing more can fold and the payload is still over window ${limit} by local estimate (~${Math.round(result.payloadEstimate)} tok, ${result.compressedRanges} range(s) folded) — no proven upstream wall on record — forwarding per #7537 (no local estimate-refusal); the upstream's own size verdict is authoritative${shrinkNote}`);\n        log(\"info\", `[${session.id}] preflight forward core-text profile: ${describeCoreTextDuplication(fwdMsgs)}`);\n        return outbound;\n    }\n    const status = f?.kind === \"upstream\" && f.status === 429 ? 503 : 502;\n    // #3918: non-deterministic exhaustion WITH committed progress is not terminal —\n    // the folds persist in the session, so the next attempt starts from a smaller\n    // baseline and continues the fold. Reporting retryable=false told hosts to stop\n    // spinning exactly where each retry makes real progress (incident: 64 effective\n    // folds, every round declared terminal). Deterministic exhaustion keeps today's\n    // verdict: nothing more can fold from this view, so retries are genuinely doomed.\n    const progressContinues = f?.kind === \"exhausted\" && !f.deterministic && result.compressedRanges > 0;\n    // #3846: a deterministic can-never-fit verdict is local refusal evidence for\n    // #2189: an explicit retryable=false from preflight (credential-shape\n    // rejection — deterministic for the identical payload) overrides the\n    // status-based heuristic below; every other path keeps today's mapping.\n    const retryable = progressContinues ? true : f?.retryable === false ? false : f?.retryable === true || (f?.kind === \"upstream\" && f.status !== undefined && (f.status === 429 || f.status >= 500));\n    let ffDetail = f?.detail ?? \"the payload still exceeds the window after preflight compression\";\n    if (progressContinues) {\n        const shortfall = foldedCalibratedSize !== undefined ? Math.max(0, limit - foldedCalibratedSize) : undefined;\n        ffDetail += ` ${result.compressedRanges} range(s) folded this turn persist in the session — the next attempt starts from a smaller baseline and continues the fold${shortfall !== undefined ? ` (~${shortfall.toLocaleString(\"en-US\")} tokens short of the target)` : \"\"}.`;\n    }\n    const ff = failFast(status, ffDetail, retryable, result.compressedRanges > 0 ? foldedCalibratedSize : undefined, result.rangesRemaining);\n    // (#4079) the #726 dead-end cooldown arming was removed with the whole\n    // mechanism — see the block comment where the walk starts. The retry\n    // contract lives entirely in this answer's retryable:false/status.\n    return ff;\n}\n\n// Host-injected contextual user fragments: machine-generated context sent as\n// USER-role messages ahead of the first real question (codex: AGENTS.md\n// instructions, environment context). Using one as the session title locks the\n// title to launch boilerplate forever (#2118). Evidence-permitlist mirroring\n// codex's own type_markers (openai/codex codex-rs/context-fragments/src/fragment.rs\n// matches_marked_text: trimmed text starts with open AND ends with close, ASCII\n// case-insensitive) — extend only with source evidence, never keyword filters.\nconst CONTEXTUAL_USER_FRAGMENT_MARKERS: ReadonlyArray<readonly [string, string]> = [\n    [\"# AGENTS.md instructions\", \"</INSTRUCTIONS>\"],\n    [\"<environment_context>\", \"</environment_context>\"],\n];\n\nfunction asciiCI(hay: string, needle: string): boolean {\n    if (hay.length !== needle.length) return false;\n    for (let i = 0; i < hay.length; i++) {\n        const h = hay.charCodeAt(i);\n        const n = needle.charCodeAt(i);\n        if (h === n) continue;\n        const hl = h >= 65 && h <= 90 ? h + 32 : h;\n        const nl = n >= 65 && n <= 90 ? n + 32 : n;\n        if (hl !== nl) return false;\n    }\n    return true;\n}\n\nexport function isContextualUserFragment(text: string): boolean {\n    const t = text.trim();\n    if (!t) return false;\n    return CONTEXTUAL_USER_FRAGMENT_MARKERS.some(([open, close]) =>\n        asciiCI(t.slice(0, open.length), open) && asciiCI(t.slice(t.length - close.length), close));\n}\n\n// Host-injected notification user fragments (dsh / deepseek-harness): machine-\n// generated notices spliced into the conversation as USER-role messages ahead\n// of the first real question — using one locks the set-once title to launch\n// boilerplate forever (#2286). Same evidence-permitlist discipline as #2118 —\n// extend only with source evidence, never keyword filters. Sources\n// (deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness, MIT):\n//   packages/interaction/user-approval/src/index.ts:\n//     `The approval policy changed from \"${previous}\" to \"${policy}\" ...`\n//   packages/core/system-prompt/src/index.ts joinContextSections +\n//   packages/core/agent-loop/src/runtime-context.ts CLEARED:\n//     `Current runtime context ...`\n//   packages/context/time-context/src/index.ts:\n//     `Time sampled while preparing turn N, step M: <ts>` — its\n//     `Browser time zone for this request:` line is embedded in that ONE\n//     message, never sent standalone, so no separate prefix for it.\n//   #7085: dsh 0.2.2-rc.3 wraps its injected notifications (the reworded\n//     runtime-context snapshot and its siblings) in a \\x3csystem-reminder\\x3e\n//     envelope; the envelope itself is the prefix — a real user question\n//     never opens with it.\nconst AUTO_INJECTED_NOTIFICATION_PREFIXES: ReadonlyArray<string> = [\n    \"The approval policy changed from\",\n    \"Current runtime context\",\n    \"Time sampled while preparing turn\",\n    \"\\x3csystem-reminder\\x3e\",\n];\n\nexport function isAutoInjectedNotification(text: string): boolean {\n    const t = text.trim();\n    if (!t) return false;\n    return AUTO_INJECTED_NOTIFICATION_PREFIXES.some((p) => asciiCI(t.slice(0, p.length), p));\n}\n\n/** Derive a short human-readable title from the first real user text message.\n *  Used so the web UI can show \"Fix auth bug\" instead of an opaque hash.\n *  Contextual fragments (#2118) and host-injected notifications (#2286) are\n *  skipped — if no real question has arrived yet, no title is set and\n *  derivation retries on later requests. */\nexport function deriveTitle(messages: CoreMessage[]): string | undefined {\n    for (const m of messages) {\n        if (m.role !== \"user\" || m.contentType !== \"text\") continue;\n        const raw = m.text ?? \"\";\n        if (!raw.trim()) continue;\n        if (isContextualUserFragment(raw)) continue;\n        if (isAutoInjectedNotification(raw)) continue;\n        const clean = raw.replace(/\\s+/g, \" \").trim();\n        return clean.length > 60 ? clean.slice(0, 57) + \"\\u2026\" : clean;\n    }\n    return undefined;\n}\n\n// #1206: orphan reaping was silent — blocks deactivated because their source\n// messages vanished from client history are the strongest runtime signal that\n// something outside bili (client auto-compaction or another compression plugin)\n// rewrote the conversation. Log it and record it in the session ledger.\nexport function reapOrphansLogged(session: Session, msgs: CoreMessage[], log: (level: string, msg: string) => void, sessionId: string): void {\n    const { reaped } = reapOrphanBlocks(session, msgs, deactivateBlock);\n    if (reaped.length === 0) return;\n    log(\"warn\", `[${sessionId}] orphan-gc deactivated ${reaped.length} block(s) whose source messages left the client history (${reaped.join(\", \")}) — the client or another compression plugin deleted summarized content; those summaries can no longer be decompressed (#1206)`);\n    recordConflict(session, \"orphan-reap\", `${reaped.length} block(s) deactivated: ${reaped.join(\", \")}`);\n}\n\nexport function headerValue(req: http.IncomingMessage, name: string): string | undefined {\n    const lower = name.toLowerCase();\n    for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(req.headers)) {\n        if (k.toLowerCase() === lower) return Array.isArray(v) ? v[0] : v;\n    }\n    return undefined;\n}\n\n/** Thrown by readBody when the request body exceeds the configured receive-body\n *  budget (limitsReceiveBytes). handle() catches this and attempts a 413 response;\n *  readBody also destroys the request socket so a client that keeps streaming a\n *  pathological body cannot hold the connection open. */\nexport class BodyTooLargeError extends Error {\n    constructor(public readonly limit: number) {\n        super(`request body exceeds ${limit} bytes`);\n        this.name = \"BodyTooLargeError\";\n    }\n}\n\nexport function readBody(req: http.IncomingMessage): Promise<Buffer> {\n    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n        const chunks: Buffer[] = [];\n        let size = 0;\n        let settled = false;\n        const cleanup = () => {\n            settled = true;\n            chunks.length = 0;\n            req.off(\"data\", onData);\n            req.off(\"end\", onEnd);\n            req.off(\"error\", onError);\n            req.off(\"close\", onClose);\n        };\n        const onError = (error: unknown) => {\n            if (settled) return;\n            cleanup();\n            reject(error);\n        };\n        const onData = (c: Buffer) => {\n            if (settled) return;\n            size += c.length;\n            const limit = knobLimitsReceiveBytes();\n            if (size > limit) {\n                onError(new BodyTooLargeError(limit));\n                req.destroy();\n                return;\n            }\n            chunks.push(c);\n        };\n        const onEnd = () => {\n            if (settled) return;\n            try {\n                const body = Buffer.concat(chunks);\n                cleanup();\n                resolve(body);\n            } catch (error) {\n                onError(error);\n            }\n        };\n        // IncomingMessage also closes after a normal end, whose handler has\n        // already settled and removed this premature-close fallback.\n        const onClose = () => onError(new Error(\"request closed before body completed\"));\n        req.on(\"data\", onData);\n        req.on(\"end\", onEnd);\n        req.on(\"error\", onError);\n        req.on(\"close\", onClose);\n    });\n}\n\nfunction logMsg(opts: ProxyOptions, level: string, msg: string): void {\n    if (!opts.log) return;\n    loggerLog(level, msg);\n}\n\nexport { getUnrecognizedPathStats, logDumpFailure, logUnrecognizedPath } from \"./server/observability.js\";\nexport { BILI_HOP_HEADER, parseLauncherModelWindows, anthropicBetaContextWindow, anthropicBetaMessageThreads, capRegistryWindowByStandard, expandedContextSuffixWindow } from \"./server/context-window.js\";\nexport { BILI_TOOL_NAMES, isAudioOutputCall, isSideRequest, isStructuredOutputCall, outputBudgetField, restoreOutputBudget, sideRequestGuard, stripLeakedBiliTools, _resetNoOutputCeilingWarningsForTest, _resetDshMidBandWarningsForTest, OUTPUT_RESTORE_ABSOLUTE_FLOOR, type OutputBudgetField } from \"./server/side-request.js\";\nexport { countSystemAndToolsTokens, estimateInputTokens, estimateWireOverhead, clampOutputBudget, emergencyNudge, projectThinkingMass, type ThinkingMassInput } from \"./server/budget.js\";\n"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/rollout.ts",
      "content": "// Feature-rollout gating (#3062): canary percentages over a stable\n// per-install identity. The mechanism this module owns:\n//\n//   1. IDENTITY — every install gets ONE random UUID, persisted under the\n//      machine-global state dir the first time any gated feature resolves\n//      (\"安装后不变\"). All lanes and copies on one machine (global install,\n//      dsh profile copy, pi tree) share the id, so a machine is exactly one\n//      cohort member — in or out consistently everywhere.\n//   2. BUCKETING — bucket = sha256(salt + \"\\n\" + id) % 10000 (basis points);\n//      enabled ⇔ bucket < percent × 100. Prefix-stable: raising the percent\n//      never drops an already-enabled install (monotonic rollout, 灰度只进\n//      不出). To re-randomize the cohort, change the salt.\n//   3. NESTING — a feature may declare `base`: it is evaluated only inside\n//      the base feature's enabled cohort (灰度 A 的用户里再灰度 B; C→D the\n//      same), so a nested percent is relative to the base population, not\n//      everyone. Base chains of any depth; cycles fail closed (off).\n//   4. PRECEDENCE — env `BILI_ROLLOUT_<FEATURE>` (\"0\"/\"false\" = off, any\n//      other value = on) > config `rollout.features.<name>.enabled` >\n//      bucketing over percent (config `percent` override > registry default).\n//      A feature absent from the registry AND from the config block is OFF.\n//\n// A release that wants to canary a feature adds one entry to ROLLOUT_FEATURES\n// (percent 0–100, optional salt/base); GA = bump to 100, or move the default\n// into the feature's own knob and drop the entry. The registry ships EMPTY —\n// no behavior change rides along with the mechanism itself; every adopter\n// declares its own entry in its own PR.\n\nimport { createHash, randomUUID } from \"node:crypto\";\nimport os from \"node:os\";\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport { stateDir } from \"./paths.js\";\nimport { loadConfigFile, type RolloutFeatureOverride, type RolloutFileConfig } from \"./config.js\";\nimport { log as loggerLog } from \"./logger.js\";\nimport { kvStore } from \"./persist.js\";\n\n/** One feature's baked-in rollout plan (version-owned, set at release time). */\nexport interface RolloutPlan {\n    /** Percent of installs, 0–100 (fractional allowed, e.g. 0.5 = 50 bp). */\n    percent: number;\n    /** Hash salt; defaults to the feature name. Changing it re-randomizes the cohort. */\n    salt?: string;\n    /** Nested rollout: evaluate this feature only inside `base`'s enabled cohort. */\n    base?: string;\n}\n\n/** Registry of features currently under rollout. EMPTY by default — adding an\n *  entry is a per-feature decision (issue + PR), never mechanical. */\nexport const ROLLOUT_FEATURES: Record<string, RolloutPlan> = {\n    // #3248 incremental turns: lets a native extension send only the delta of\n    // a conversation (marker `x-bili-plugin-turn` on ordinary model requests)\n    // once enabled for this install. Default 0% — every client keeps the\n    // byte-identical full-resend behavior. Operators force it on with\n    // `rollout.features.pluginIncrementalTurns: true` (or a percent), or\n    // `BILI_ROLLOUT_PLUGIN_INCREMENTAL_TURNS=1`.\n    pluginIncrementalTurns: { percent: 0 },\n    // #5403/#5418 full-resend watermark fastpath: plugin-lane turns re-send\n    // the ENTIRE history each turn; on a verified hit (count watermark\n    // stamped by the previous response) the server stops re-parsing and\n    // re-materializing the identical prefix and decodes only head + new tail.\n    // Every verification miss degrades to the legacy full-parse path\n    // byte-identically. EXPERIMENTAL grey rollout at 5% (owner ruling\n    // 2026-11-02: default off, small cohort first, web switch + one-time\n    // intro notice ship alongside); force it per install with\n    // `rollout.features.pluginFullResendWatermark: true|false` (or a percent)\n    // / `BILI_ROLLOUT_PLUGIN_FULL_RESEND_WATERMARK=1|0`.\n    pluginFullResendWatermark: { percent: 5 },\n    // #4804 WS delta continuation: codex/opencode WebSocket clients that keep a\n    // previous_response_id checkpoint stop reconstructing full history on every\n    // turn — the session augments the delta with the server-committed previous\n    // output and the outbound prefix renders from the unified transcript\n    // (anchored snapshot render). Every verification miss degrades to the\n    // legacy full-reconstruction path or the 400 the client answers with a\n    // full replay (lossless). Requires storage.unified=full (reads); default\n    // 0% — force on with `rollout.features.wsDeltaContinuation: true` or\n    // `BILI_ROLLOUT_WS_DELTA_CONTINUATION=1`.\n    wsDeltaContinuation: { percent: 0 },\n    // #2926 anthropic Threads reforge: when the mirrored thread history\n    // crosses the window on a `continue`, swap it for a fresh `create`\n    // carrying [summary, tail ring, delta]. Default 0% — threads traffic\n    // stays byte-faithful passthrough. Mirror capture itself is always on\n    // wherever the unified sidecar is available. Force on with\n    // `rollout.features.anthropicThreadsReforge: true` or\n    // `BILI_ROLLOUT_ANTHROPIC_THREADS_REFORGE=1`.\n    anthropicThreadsReforge: { percent: 0 },\n    // #3756 snapshot render: assemble the outbound prefix from the server-side\n    // canonical transcript (unified storage) instead of re-deriving message\n    // identity from client-resent bytes, making folded sessions immune to\n    // codec/identity upgrades (#3752) and to client-side head\n    // deletion/checkpointing (#3723). Degrades to the legacy path whenever the\n    // rollout is off or the unified transcript cannot resolve. Default 0% —\n    // force on with `BILI_ROLLOUT_SNAPSHOT_RENDER=1`.\n    snapshotRender: { percent: 0 },\n    // #4491 plugin-lane server history: pin message identity to client-supplied\n    // message ids (the `biliMsgIds` body field on plugin-wire traffic) and\n    // serve the outbound prefix from the server-owned transcript\n    // (POST /__bili/plugin/render). The id-set algebra classifies vanishing\n    // cohorts (compressed vs deleted) and detects generation switches.\n    // Default 0% — force on with `BILI_ROLLOUT_PLUGIN_LANE_SERVER_HISTORY=1`.\n    pluginLaneServerHistory: { percent: 0 },\n    // #5825 identity-channel harvest seam (registry in identity-harvest.ts):\n    // loopback clients without an explicit body channel get stable session+\n    // message identity aligned from their OWN local transcript/sqlite\n    // (claude-code / codebuddy / mcode adapters). The per-install env switch\n    // BILI_IDENTITY_HARVEST alone already enables it; this key exists for a\n    // COHORT-WIDE ramp that never touches anyone's env. Decoupled from\n    // pluginLaneServerHistory on purpose (owner ruling 2026-11-07): that flag\n    // governs whether stamped ids get PINNED to rows, this one governs where\n    // the seam may even read local files — coupling them made opting one's\n    // own install in require bumping an unrelated rollout. Default 0%.\n    identityChannelHarvest: { percent: 0 },\n    // #7168/#7439 DSH client-extension intercept: DSH (deepseek-harness) rides\n    // top-level `dsh_*` fields on every request — `dsh_session_log` (the 8 MiB\n    // lossless session-log upload for the official DeepSeek API; the model never\n    // reads it) plus the sibling `dsh_plugin_packages`. On forked/seeded sessions\n    // it resends the whole log each turn until its watermark catches up. Default\n    // 0% = INTERCEPT: bili strips top-level `dsh_*` from the inbound body\n    // (handle.ts) so the 8 MiB is never forwarded upstream — no bandwidth waste,\n    // no unknown-field risk on a non-DeepSeek upstream. DSH self-heals because its\n    // upload watermark only advances on a 2xx (llm-deepseek/adapter.ts), which bili\n    // still returns; the window meter is separately exempt (#7168 dsh_* skip).\n    // RELEASE once the server-authoritative egress work (#6785 / discussion #7439)\n    // ships the client-extension sideband — flip this to 100% (or remove the strip)\n    // and DSH's official-DeepSeek session-log upload resumes. Force pass-through\n    // now with `rollout.features.passDshExtensions: true` /\n    // `BILI_ROLLOUT_PASS_DSH_EXTENSIONS=1`.\n    passDshExtensions: { percent: 0 },\n    // #7439 — stamped session-id identity: the server trusts the client's stamped\n    // session id + purpose and stops content-guessing subagent forks (the |sub:…\n    // ladder in session-resolve.ts). GA — ON by default (owner ruling 2026-11-22):\n    // the stamped id is battle-tested across the dsh/claude/codex lanes. The #5095\n    // client-declared subagent lane-token tail is NOT gated (it is the declared\n    // \"tail\" path, not a guess). Force OFF only to debug the legacy ladder, with\n    // BILI_ROLLOUT_TRUST_STAMPED_ID=0 or `rollout.features.trustStampedId: false`.\n    trustStampedId: { percent: 100 },\n};\n\nexport const BP_MAX = 10_000;\n\nexport type RolloutSource = \"env\" | \"config\" | \"bucket\" | \"off\";\n\nexport interface RolloutDecision {\n    feature: string;\n    enabled: boolean;\n    /** Which tier decided: env override | config enabled | bucket math | not under rollout at all. */\n    source: RolloutSource;\n    /** The install's bucket for this feature's salt, [0, 10000). */\n    bucket: number;\n    /** The percent actually applied (basis points), for diagnostics. */\n    percentBp: number;\n    salt: string;\n    base?: string;\n}\n\n/** Env var for one feature: `BILI_ROLLOUT_` + name as UPPER_SNAKE\n *  (camelCase / kebab-case both fold: \"simhashV2\" and \"fold-guard\" →\n *  BILI_ROLLOUT_SIMHASH_V2 / BILI_ROLLOUT_FOLD_GUARD). */\nexport function rolloutEnvName(feature: string): string {\n    return \"BILI_ROLLOUT_\" + feature\n        .replace(/([a-z0-9])([A-Z])/g, \"$1_$2\")\n        .replace(/[-\\s]+/g, \"_\")\n        .replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9_]/g, \"\")\n        .toUpperCase();\n}\n\n/** Deterministic bucket for (salt, id): sha256 → uint32 → [0, 10000). */\nexport function rolloutBucket(salt: string, id: string): number {\n    return createHash(\"sha256\").update(`${salt}\\n${id}`).digest().readUInt32BE(0) % BP_MAX;\n}\n\n/** Clamp a user/config percent into basis points; invalid → undefined. */\nfunction percentBp(v: unknown): number | undefined {\n    if (typeof v !== \"number\" || !Number.isFinite(v) || v < 0 || v > 100) return undefined;\n    return Math.min(BP_MAX, Math.round(v * 100));\n}\n\nexport interface RolloutCtx {\n    /** Bucketing identity (the install id, or an explicit test override). */\n    id: string;\n    env?: NodeJS.ProcessEnv;\n    /** Config tier; defaults to loadConfigFile().rollout. */\n    file?: RolloutFileConfig;\n}\n\nfunction overrideFor(feature: string, file: RolloutFileConfig | undefined): RolloutFeatureOverride {\n    const features = file?.features;\n    if (!features || typeof features !== \"object\" || Array.isArray(features)) return {};\n    const o = features[feature];\n    // Shorthand forms users naturally write first: `x: true/false` = force\n    // on/off, `x: 20` = percent 20. Dropping these silently (the object-only\n    // read) left users believing they had forced a feature while the bucket\n    // math still decided — flagged in #3062 review; keep every shorthand\n    // meaningful instead of erroring.\n    if (o === true) return { enabled: true };\n    if (o === false) return { enabled: false };\n    if (typeof o === \"number\" && Number.isFinite(o)) return { percent: o };\n    return o && typeof o === \"object\" && !Array.isArray(o) ? o : {};\n}\n\n/** #5403 watermark intro notice: true when the user's file carries NO\n *  explicit override for the feature (neither shorthand nor object field —\n *  a salt/base-only entry still counts as having touched the knob), so a\n *  user who already made the call is never nagged. */\nexport function featureOverrideAbsent(feature: string, file: RolloutFileConfig | undefined): boolean {\n    return Object.keys(overrideFor(feature, file)).length === 0;\n}\n\nfunction resolveInternal(feature: string, ctx: RolloutCtx, visited: Set<string>): RolloutDecision {\n    const env = ctx.env ?? process.env;\n    const file = ctx.file ?? loadConfigFile().rollout;\n    const o = overrideFor(feature, file);\n    const plan = ROLLOUT_FEATURES[feature];\n    const salt = typeof o.salt === \"string\" && o.salt.length > 0 ? o.salt : plan?.salt ?? feature;\n    const base = typeof o.base === \"string\" && o.base.length > 0 ? o.base : plan?.base;\n    const bucket = rolloutBucket(salt, ctx.id);\n    const percent = percentBp(o.percent) ?? (plan ? percentBp(plan.percent) : undefined);\n\n    const decided = (enabled: boolean, source: RolloutSource): RolloutDecision => ({\n        feature, enabled, source, bucket,\n        percentBp: percent ?? 0, salt, base,\n    });\n\n    // Tier 1: env force. \"0\"/\"false\" = off, anything else set = on (same\n    // family as BILI_PERSIST / ACP_PASSTHROUGH).\n    const envRaw = env[rolloutEnvName(feature)];\n    if (envRaw !== undefined) return decided(envRaw !== \"0\" && envRaw !== \"false\", \"env\");\n\n    // Tier 2: explicit config boolean — overrides any percentage.\n    if (o.enabled === true) return decided(true, \"config\");\n    if (o.enabled === false) return decided(false, \"config\");\n\n    // Tier 3: bucketing. No percent from anywhere → the feature is not under\n    // rollout → OFF (fail closed; unknown features never leak on).\n    if (percent === undefined) return decided(false, \"off\");\n\n    // Nested rollout: only installs already inside `base`'s cohort are\n    // candidates. Cycles fail closed instead of looping.\n    if (base !== undefined) {\n        if (visited.has(base)) return decided(false, \"off\");\n        const baseDecision = resolveInternal(base, ctx, visited.add(feature));\n        if (!baseDecision.enabled) return decided(false, \"off\");\n    }\n    return decided(bucket < percent, \"bucket\");\n}\n\n/** Resolve one feature's rollout decision (pure over its ctx). */\nexport function resolveRollout(feature: string, ctx: RolloutCtx): RolloutDecision {\n    return resolveInternal(feature, ctx, new Set());\n}\n\n/** Decisions for every registered feature (startup log / diagnostics). */\nexport function rolloutDecisions(id: string): RolloutDecision[] {\n    return Object.keys(ROLLOUT_FEATURES).sort().map((f) => resolveRollout(f, { id }));\n}\n\n// --- stable per-install identity --------------------------------------------\n\n/** Resolve+create the install id file. Cached per resolved path so test seams\n *  relocating XDG_STATE_HOME get independent ids within one process. */\nconst idCache = new Map<string, string>();\n\n// #5753: the identity rides the UNIFIED storage (kv_store namespace \"rollout\",\n// key \"install-id\") under the #5548 carrier rules: kv primary once hydrated,\n// legacy file kept as pre-hydration fallback + sole carrier on legacy-only\n// instances + fresh-install BOOTSTRAP. The bootstrap matters: two lane copies\n// racing on a brand-new install must converge on ONE id (the historical wx\n// create-file race is the tie-breaker), so generation still creates the file\n// exactly once per install lifetime; every later read/write goes to kv.\nconst ID_NS = \"rollout\";\nconst ID_KEY = \"install-id\";\nlet kvInstallId: string | null = null;\nlet kvIdHydrated = false;\nlet kvIdWarned = false;\n\nfunction kvIdWarnOnce(tag: string, err: unknown): void {\n    if (kvIdWarned) return;\n    kvIdWarned = true;\n    loggerLog(\"warn\", `[rollout] ${tag} failed — install id stays file-based for this process: ${err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err)}`);\n}\n\n/** Once per process (wired at cli start): adopt the unified-storage id when\n *  present, otherwise import the legacy file into kv one time. Never throws.\n */\nexport async function hydrateRolloutIdentity(): Promise<void> {\n    const store = kvStore();\n    if (kvIdHydrated || !store) return;\n    try {\n        const doc = await store.getKvAsync(ID_NS, ID_KEY);\n        const v = doc && typeof doc === \"object\" ? ((doc as { id?: unknown })[\"id\"] as unknown) : undefined;\n        if (typeof v === \"string\" && /^[0-9a-f-]{8,}$/i.test(v)) {\n            kvInstallId = v;\n            kvIdHydrated = true;\n            return;\n        }\n        // no usable row: import the legacy file (one-time migration).\n        const file = rolloutIdFile();\n        const fileCached = idCache.get(file) ?? readIdFile(file);\n        if (fileCached !== undefined) {\n            await store.setKvAsync(ID_NS, ID_KEY, { id: fileCached });\n            kvInstallId = fileCached;\n            idCache.set(file, fileCached);\n            loggerLog(\"info\", `[rollout] imported the install id from the legacy JSON file into unified storage (kv_store namespace \"${ID_NS}\")`);\n        }\n        kvIdHydrated = true;\n    } catch (err) {\n        kvIdWarnOnce(\"hydrate\", err);\n    }\n}\n\nfunction rolloutIdFile(): string {\n    return path.join(stateDir(), \"rollout-id.json\");\n}\n\nfunction readIdFile(file: string): string | undefined {\n    try {\n        const parsed = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(file, \"utf8\")) as { id?: unknown };\n        return typeof parsed.id === \"string\" && /^[0-9a-f-]{8,}$/i.test(parsed.id) ? parsed.id : undefined;\n    } catch {\n        return undefined;\n    }\n}\n\n/** The stable rollout identity for this machine: config `rollout.installId`\n *  when pinned (support/testing), else the persisted state-dir UUID. On an\n *  unwritable state dir the fallback derives from the home+host — stable\n *  across restarts even when nothing can be persisted. */\nexport function rolloutInstallId(): string {\n    const pinned = loadConfigFile().rollout?.installId;\n    if (typeof pinned === \"string\" && pinned.trim().length > 0) return pinned.trim();\n    const file = rolloutIdFile();\n    const cached = idCache.get(file);\n    if (cached !== undefined) return cached;\n    if (kvInstallId !== null) {\n        idCache.set(file, kvInstallId);\n        return kvInstallId;\n    }\n    const existing = readIdFile(file);\n    if (existing !== undefined) {\n        idCache.set(file, existing);\n        return existing;\n    }\n    const generated = randomUUID();\n    try {\n        fs.mkdirSync(path.dirname(file), { recursive: true });\n        // \"wx\": concurrent processes race to create exactly one file; losers\n        // keep the winner's id, so the identity stays single-valued. A file\n        // that EXISTS but does not parse (hand-mangled) is healed in place with\n        // the fresh id — next boot is stable again on whichever write won.\n        try {\n            fs.writeFileSync(file, JSON.stringify({ id: generated }, null, 2) + \"\\n\", { flag: \"wx\" });\n        } catch (e) {\n            if ((e as NodeJS.ErrnoException).code !== \"EEXIST\") throw e;\n            if (readIdFile(file) === undefined) {\n                loggerLog(\"warn\", `[rollout] install id file ${file} is unreadable — regenerating`);\n                fs.writeFileSync(file, JSON.stringify({ id: generated }, null, 2) + \"\\n\");\n            }\n        }\n    } catch (e) {\n        loggerLog(\"warn\", `[rollout] cannot persist install id (${String(e)}) — falling back to a derived id`);\n        // os lookups can throw on exotic hosts (uid with no passwd entry,\n        // ENOSYS hostname) — the fallback itself must never take boot down.\n        let hostname = \"\";\n        let username = \"\";\n        try { hostname = os.hostname(); } catch { /* degraded: \"\" */ }\n        try { username = os.userInfo().username; } catch { /* degraded: \"\" */ }\n        const derived = derivedInstallId(process.env.HOME ?? process.env.USERPROFILE ?? \"\", hostname, username);\n        idCache.set(file, derived);\n        return derived;\n    }\n    const settled = readIdFile(file) ?? generated;\n    // #5753: once the identity is settled, it lives in the unified store; the\n    // file remains only as the cross-process bootstrap artifact written above.\n    // (kvStore(): suites may install partial stubs — never call methods that\n    // are absent on them.)\n    const kvs = kvStore();\n    if (kvs && kvInstallId === null) {\n        void kvs\n            .setKvAsync(ID_NS, ID_KEY, { id: settled })\n            .then(() => { if (kvInstallId === null) kvInstallId = settled; })\n            .catch((err) => kvIdWarnOnce(\"persist\", err));\n    }\n    idCache.set(file, settled);\n    return settled;\n}\n\n/** Deterministic fallback id for hosts where the state dir cannot be written.\n * Cross-platform on purpose: os.hostname() (NOT process.env.HOSTNAME, which\n * is a bash-ism and is absent on Windows — every such Windows box used to\n * collide on one shared derived id and move through cohorts in lockstep),\n * the OS home (USERPROFILE on Windows), and the local user name. Same inputs\n * → same id across restarts, so the cohort stays sticky even on this path. */\nexport function derivedInstallId(home: string, hostname: string, username: string): string {\n    return \"derived-\" + createHash(\"sha256\").update(`${username}\\n${hostname}\\n${home}`).digest(\"hex\").slice(0, 32);\n}\n\n/** Test seam: drop the unified-identity caches. */\nexport function _resetRolloutIdentityForTest(): void {\n    kvInstallId = null;\n    kvIdHydrated = false;\n    kvIdWarned = false;\n    // a simulated restart re-resolves every carrier — the file-keyed identity\n    // cache must not leak a wiped volume's id into the \"fresh\" process.\n    idCache.clear();\n}\n\n/** One feature's effective gate, against the real install id. Call sites use\n *  this exactly where the feature's default would otherwise be a plain\n *  boolean. Resolves per call: env/config hot-edits flip without a restart. */\nexport function featureEnabled(feature: string): boolean {\n    return resolveRollout(feature, { id: rolloutInstallId() }).enabled;\n}\n\n// #2607-style warn-once for rollout config that silently does nothing:\n// unknown features with no resolvable force, non-object entries the resolver\n// must ignore, and wrong-typed enabled/percent that fail strict equality /\n// percentBp and fall back to the bucket without a word (\"enabled\": \"true\").\n// Every one of these used to no-op silently — the user believed the force\n// had taken hold while the bucket still decided (#3062 review).\nlet warnedInertSignature: string | null = null;\nexport function warnRolloutConfigProblems(): void {\n    const file = loadConfigFile().rollout;\n    const features = file?.features;\n    if (!features || typeof features !== \"object\" || Array.isArray(features)) return;\n    const problems: string[] = [];\n    for (const [name, raw] of Object.entries(features).sort(([a], [b]) => a.localeCompare(b))) {\n        // Shorthands accepted by overrideFor are real config — except a\n        // number outside 0–100, which percentBp rejects: the value would be\n        // dropped with zero feedback (silent OFF, or silent fall-back to the\n        // baked-in plan), so name it like every other ignored entry.\n        if (raw === true || raw === false) continue;\n        if (typeof raw === \"number\") {\n            if (percentBp(raw) !== undefined) continue;\n            problems.push(`${name} (ignored: must be a number 0–100, got ${JSON.stringify(raw)})`);\n            continue;\n        }\n        if (!raw || typeof raw !== \"object\" || Array.isArray(raw)) {\n            problems.push(`${name} (ignored: not an override object — use {enabled: true}, {percent: 20}, true, false, or a bare number)`);\n            continue;\n        }\n        if (ROLLOUT_FEATURES[name] === undefined && raw.enabled === undefined && percentBp(raw.percent) === undefined) {\n            problems.push(`${name} (no effect: feature not under rollout in this version — typo? not yet shipped here?)`);\n            continue;\n        }\n        if (raw.enabled !== undefined && typeof raw.enabled !== \"boolean\") {\n            problems.push(`${name}.enabled (ignored: must be a boolean, got ${typeof raw.enabled} — quotes around true/false?)`);\n        }\n        if (raw.percent !== undefined && percentBp(raw.percent) === undefined) {\n            problems.push(`${name}.percent (ignored: must be a number 0–100, got ${JSON.stringify(raw.percent)})`);\n        }\n    }\n    if (problems.length === 0) return;\n    const signature = problems.join(\"\\u0000\");\n    if (warnedInertSignature === signature) return;\n    warnedInertSignature = signature;\n    loggerLog(\"warn\", `[rollout] config problems — these entries do nothing until fixed: ${problems.join(\"; \")}`);\n}\n"
